nd over  again he's disgusted by the idea and his  feelings and loyalties undergo a drastic  change that swing is made even more  pronounced when Queen Allison summons  him he reveals the truth and asks her to  give him the death penalty rather than  sentence him to gelding and torture sir  Kristen was right to worry we know for  Martin's writing that the kingsguard is  a lifetime appointment and punishment  for those who break their vows as  castration followed by a lifetime  sentence at the wall that Allison shows  Kristen Mercy both during his  questioning and in his moment of  hopelessness when he nearly takes his  own life will have made a strong  impression as a Targaryen without a  dragon king viserys is something of an  outlier so far we've seen Damon on  karaxi's rhaenyra on Cyrax and Lenor  who's half Targaryen on sea smoke  princess rhaenice is the most senior  Targaryen with the most Dragon riding  experience and in episode 5 we finally  get to see her mounted on her Dragon  Fire and Blood tells us that the dragon  is named melies and is also known as the  Red Queen so named for the beautiful  Rosy tint of her wings and scales she's  faster than karaxi's and originally  belonged to pasaris and Damon's mother  Queen Alyssa and both then princes took  their first dragon rides upon her back  when they were only days old the young  princess toured the Seven Kingdoms with  her grandfather King J Harris and she  rode the red queen to her own wedding  with Corliss when she was only about 16  years old it's a nice touch that the  show has her riding alongside Lenor and  route to her son's nuptials iron blood  is a fictional collected history  compiled from different sources who were  privy to different events in different  ways and who each had their own  political point of view and allegiances  the narrator whose accounts are often  the most detailed in scandalous is  mushroom a dwarf who served as fool to  King viserys's Court his physical  appearance three feet tall with an  oversized head and position as fool led  many in the nobility to assume that he  was intellectually disabled but he was  actually Savvy and observant fans of  Fire and Blood have had their fingers  crossed that we might get to see  mushroom as a character in House of the  Dragon no announcements to that effect  have been made however there is a  background character who fits mushroom's  description during rhaenyra and lenor's  wedding festivities he's wearing  Targaryen colors and playing music with  the rest of a band which is close enough  to a court jester he's even featured in  the teaser for episode 5. this is  probably just a wink to book readers but  our mystery man could come back to  record a story it's worth mentioning  that mushroom was quite fond of brain  era and thus his version would be  inclined to put her in a more favorable  light the costume in on House of the  Dragon isn't commended able just for its  stunning design and impeccable  construction the attire worn by King's  Landings movers and shakers is  significant and symbolic in Martin's  writing and so far the show is doing a  phenomenal job of illustrating that  I understand the queen is still readying  herself for the celebrations the single  most consequential piece of clothing  with literal life and death consequences  is Allison's green dress which makes its  debut in episode 5. she interrupts her  husband's wedding toast and Cat walks  through the throne room in an Exquisite  emerald green gown pulling all the  attention away from the rainian Monarch  in the air and bride to be Lara strong  asks his brother if he remembers what  color house Hightower uses in its Beacon  to call its people to war the answer is  green that means with this dress alicent  is effectively using fashion to fire the  first shots in the coming Targaryen  Civil War it's our unofficial  Proclamation that she does in fact want  her son aegon to be king the occasion  for which she wears the dress is 